        "alt": "ELE_net courses in East Africa"
      }
    ],
    "body": {
      "type": "doc",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "In addition to the online courses that AKU students in East Africa can take to help them develop their academic writing skills in English, ELE_net has been offering blended courses to address specific students' needs."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "In 2018, IED students in Dar es Salaam had the opportunity to take the Language Accuracy in Writing and the Integrating Academic Reading into Writing courses through a blended approach - a mix of face-to-face teaching and online study. Also, following a recent ELE_net visit to Uganda and Kenya, the Network is now remotely delivering courses specifically tailored to SONAM students in Nairobi. These include academic reading and writing, and a new English for Presentations course, which will be offered to students during the last year of their bachelor's degree."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
